 Overview 
Houlihan Lokey, Inc. (NYSE:HLI) is a leading global investment bank recognized for delivering independent strategic and financial advice to corporations, financial sponsors, and governments. With uniquely deep industry expertise, broad international reach, and a partnership approach rooted in trust, the firm provides innovative, integrated solutions across mergers and acquisitions, capital solutions, financial restructuring, and financial and valuation advisory. Our unmatched transaction volumes provide differentiated, data-driven perspectives that help our clients achieve their most critical goals. To learn more about Houlihan Lokey, please visit HL.com.
 Capital Solutions 
Houlihan Lokey’s Capital Solutions Group was named World’s Best and Europe’s Best for Capital Markets Advisory at the Euromoney Awards for Excellence 2026. The group comprises more than 235 professionals globally and offers clients a broad range of tailored financing alternatives and strategic financial advice. Our team has raised ~$37bn across over 140 transactions in the last twelve months*and has a presence in 18 offices and 8 countries globally. With deep expertise in both private and public markets, we are committed to delivering innovative, value-enhancing solutions that support long-term success for our clients.
 Houlihan Lokey’s Secondaries Advisory Group provides strategic advice and execution services to private equity sponsors and institutional investors navigating the fast-growing market for private equity secondary transactions. The group specializes in both LP-led and GP-led transactions. Members of the Secondaries Advisory Group work with a wide variety of private equity sponsors and institutional investors - across both industry and strategy – and work in tandem with Houlihan Lokey’s industry coverage, M&A and financial & valuation advisory.
 You will 
• Work side-by-side with a talented, dedicated staff of senior professionals who will provide broad exposure to the many different considerations affecting private equity liquidity needs;
• Assist with evaluating and structuring customized financing alternatives for private equity sponsors, institutional investors, and their portfolio companies;
• Gain hands-on transaction experience by playing an integral role on deal teams from the initial pitch through closing;
• Prepare marketing materials and buyer diligence materials for LP-led and GP-led secondary transactions;
• Support the transaction execution process, including the management of virtual data rooms, tracking buyer interactions and client communications, and coordinating buyer due diligence in competitive auction
 Qualifications 
• Currently enrolled in a Master’s program with a focus on finance or management, at a top tier business school or university;
• Experience in private equity, investment banking, or a related field;
• Strong analytical skills with the ability to solve problems through data-driven analysis, combined with a high level of attention to detail;
• Pro-active and resourceful attitude of solving problems independently, with the support of an experienced senior team;
• Ability to multitask and coordinate a variety of different projects with an organized approach;
• Solid understanding of private equity fundamentals, including current market dynamics, deal structures, and competitive landscape;
• Fluency in French and English, additional languages are a plus;
•

We are global private markets specialists delivering tailored investment solutions, advisory services, and impactful, data driven insights to the world’s investors. Leveraging the power of our platform and our peerless intelligence across sectors, strategies, and geographies, we help identify the advantages and the answers our clients need to succeed. 
 The Analyst will be an integral part of StepStone's Private Equity Secondaries investment team, which recently closed its fifth fund with $7.4 billion of total capital commitments. StepStone deploys billions of dollars per year in private equity secondary deals, including GP-led transactions, LP interests in private equity funds and structured secondary deals (e.g., team spin-outs, direct investments, fund recapitalizations and other special situations).
 StepStone prides itself on the firm’s collegial atmosphere, encouraging team-building initiatives and a collaborative approach. The position will have exposure to all levels of the firm globally, from Partners to fellow Analysts, on a daily basis.
 Position Overview: 
 Your main responsibility will be to contribute to all aspects of the secondary deal process, including:
• 
 Sourcing, screening and conducting due diligence on European private equity secondary investments (both LP and GP-led transactions);
• Interact with management teams and fund managers to conduct in-depth asset and portfolio-level analysis;
• Perform quantitative and qualitative research and financial modelling/analysis on companies and assets across stages, industries and geographies;
• Preparation and presentation of due diligence materials and investment committee memos;
• Construct an opinion around various investment opportunities and efficiently communicate both verbally and in written materials; with the ability to defend your position in a team environment, including investment committee meetings;
• Support negotiation/coordination of deal closing/structuring process and post-close monitoring of existing investments; and
• Occasionally travel for onsite due diligence and to sponsor’s annual meetings to monitor investments.
 Requirements: 
• Stellar academic record (university and GPA);
• 
 1-2 years of private equity, top-tier investment banking and/or consulting experience;
• Excellent quantitative skills, including financial modelling, analytical and valuation skills for purpose of evaluating investment opportunities;
• 
 Strong sense of risk/reward trade-offs, and an ability to display sound investment judgement;
• 
 Strong appetite for self-directed learning, particularly in AI/automation, with demonstrated hands-on experimentation preferred; 
• Self-starter, with strong ability to think creativity and conduct research to solve problems or find solutions;
• Ability to communicate and present ideas effectively, both verbally and in writing;
• Capable of multi-tasking with strong attention to detail;
• Promote and demonstrate a positive, team-oriented attitude, with desire to work on various projects; and
• Fluent (written and spoken) English; (additional language skills a plus).
